 "about": "Scanned CC0 textures from ambientCG (ambientcg.com, CC0: free for any use). Tools/fetch_textures.py downloads them here (the images aren't in git); Tools/ue_build_level.py builds the land and road materials from the roles. 'tile_m' is how many metres one repeat covers. The stone roles are for the walls, scars, boulders and barns (Tools/buttertubs_stone.py): 'stone' lichened limestone, 'stone_bare' bare bedded limestone, 'moss' for the moss on them. A role's optional 'ue' block names textures already in the project (Megascans from Fab, which aren't in git); the CC0 'id' is the fallback when they're missing. 'masonry' is the rubble walling of the houses and barns.",
